# This is a TEMPLATE, not a real settings file. The app doesn't read this
# file directly — it's just an example showing what a real ".env" file
# should look like.
#
# HOW TO USE THIS:
# 1. Make a copy of this file and rename the copy to exactly ".env"
#    (no "example" in the name).
# 2. Replace the placeholder text below with your real, secret key.
# 3. Never share your real .env file or paste its contents anywhere public
#    (chat, GitHub, Slack) — it's meant to stay private on your computer.
#    The .gitignore file already makes sure Git won't ever upload it.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key-here
# ^ This is the password-like key that lets our app talk to Claude (the
#   AI) to write outreach messages. Get your real one from Anthropic's
#   website and paste it here in place of the placeholder text.
